# Roles & Permissions

## Zulip Role Hierarchy

```
Owner (100) > Admin (200) > Moderator (300) > Member (400) > Guest (600)
```

**NOTE**: Zulip API codes 100=Owner, 200=Admin (not the other way around!).

## Usage

```typescript
import { UserRole, parseRole, hasPermission, canEditMessage, canDeleteMessage, getRoleLabel, getRoleColor } from "~/shared/lib/roles";

// Parse from Zulip API response
const role = parseRole(user.role); // 200 → UserRole.Admin

// Check permission
if (hasPermission(role, "message:delete:any")) { /* admin+ */ }
if (hasPermission(role, "channel:create")) { /* member+ */ }

// Check for message UI
const showEdit = canEditMessage(role, isOwnMessage);
const showDelete = canDeleteMessage(role, isOwnMessage);

// Display
getRoleLabel(role);  // "Administrator"
getRoleColor(role);  // "text-indicator-pink" (Tailwind class)
```

## Permission Map

| Permission | Min. role | Description |
|-----------|-----------|-------------|
| `message:send` | Guest | Send messages |
| `message:edit:own` | Guest | Edit own messages |
| `message:delete:own` | Member | Delete own messages |
| `message:edit:any` | Admin | Edit others' messages |
| `message:delete:any` | Admin | Delete others' messages |
| `message:move` | Moderator | Move messages |
| `message:pin` | Moderator | Pin messages |
| `channel:create` | Member | Create channels |
| `channel:delete` | Admin | Delete channels |
| `channel:edit` | Admin | Edit channels |
| `channel:subscribe:others` | Admin | Subscribe others |
| `topic:create` | Member | Create topics |
| `topic:mute` | Guest | Mute topics |
| `topic:resolve` | Moderator | Mark topics resolved |
| `user:invite` | Admin | Invite users |
| `user:deactivate` | Admin | Deactivate users |
| `user:change-role` | Owner | Change roles |
| `org:settings` | Admin | Organization settings |

## Rules for AI Agent

### When implementing UI elements

- Action buttons (edit, delete, pin) → check `canEditMessage()` / `hasPermission()` before rendering
- Context menu → filter actions by `hasPermission(userRole, permission)`
- Admin panels → wrap in `if (hasRole(userRole, UserRole.Admin))`

### When fetching data from the API

```typescript
// GET /users or GET /users/me returns role: number
const user = await fetchCurrentUser();
const role = parseRole(user.role);  // number → UserRole enum
```

### Guest Role

- Can see and write ONLY to channels they are subscribed to
- Cannot see the full list of channels and users
- Cannot create channels or delete messages
- UI: hide creation buttons, show a limited menu
